Subject: Turns on deferred reference counting with a zero-count table

What this does
  Turns on deferred reference counting with a zero-count table.

Why we need it
  The register VM frees a value the moment its count hits zero, but a register that still holds it is about to be overwritten; so a zero-count table can park those values and a reconcile pass can free only the ones no register refers to.

What it adds
  `JSMallocBlockHeader.in_zct`, `JSRuntime.zct`/`zct_len`/`zct_cap`/`zct_nobj`/`zct_limit`/`drc_in_reconcile`, `js_free_value_rt` parks at zero, `js_drc_push`/`js_drc_zero`/`js_drc_pin`/`js_drc_unpin`/`js_drc_reconcile(_locked)`/`js_drc_safepoint`, `JS_RunGC` runs pin/reconcile/gc/unpin, safepoints from `__js_poll_interrupts` and `JS_Call` returning to C, `JS_FreeRuntime` reconciles and frees the table; `QJS_DRC_VALIDATE` builds additionally assert every counted register value is still owned.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
